id: pm-rl-kq4f
title: Repair the legacy training receipt check for the pm-toolchain update
description: "Reproduce the focused durable-loop failure on Dependabot PR 114, preserve evidence and candidate-drift assertions, and adapt only the dependency contract that changed."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,dependabot,"gh:unbraind/pm-rl#114"
created_at: "2026-10-28T19:41:30.408Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T20:05:15.114Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T19:42:12.054Z",codex-agent,"The bumped SDK causes the legacy bandit receipt test to JSON.parse an absent item.body. Reproduce the single failing case, inspect the SDK read projection contract, and request exactly the persisted evidence needed without weakening drift detection. Main is already an ancestor of the Dependabot head."
  "2026-10-28T19:45:41.145Z",codex-agent,"Cause class: dependency read-contract incompatibility in the test fixture. The default SDK token budget omits the large training receipt body. Request depth standard with outputLimit and outputBudget unbounded for this single evidence read; explicitly assert the body exists. The existing evidence verification, promotion count and candidate-drift refusal assertions are retained. The original focused test fails with JSON.parse(undefined); the updated pm-linked focused test passes 1/1."
  "2026-10-28T19:48:33.233Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable source copy: removing only the explicit body-read options makes the complete persisted body assertion fail. Restoring the options passes the focused regression 1/1, including legacy replay and candidate-drift refusal. The fixed test also passed 1/1 through the pinned pm runner in a real non-git tracker. No production logic or release threshold changed."
  "2026-10-28T19:50:10.174Z",codex-agent,"Repair CI evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/40757694370. Focused regression passed 1/1 and both disposable revert/restoration outcomes were verified. Changelog regeneration and changelog:check passed. The CI matrix must provide npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds on the final pushed head; no full-gate pass is claimed while queued."
  "2026-10-28T20:05:15.097Z",codex-agent,"The first repair CI exposed a TypeScript SDK result-union error in the new explicit-budget call. Added an item-in-result assertion before accessing the receipt, preserving fail-closed behavior. npm run build followed by npm run build:test now passes; the focused runtime regression is being repeated. This is the same scoped read-contract repair, not a threshold change."
